49	 * the user who opened a claim cannot approve it. The user who last edited a claim (through its form or
50	 * its row's amount) can neither settle nor approve it, as its opener cannot. A PENDING claim is not bound by a statement: it
51	 * shows its live figure, and is bound again by the last statement once rejected. An overdue claim's due gains a late charge on its
52	 * figure (see {@link LateCharge}), and the floor is applied last: a claim's live due is never below
53	 * the sheet's floor. A statement binds only the rate figure, not the charge nor the floor, and settling fixes the charge into the settled due. A claim with
54	 * a negative amount is a correction: it is allowed only when it names, by number, a SETTLED claim
55	 * of the same person that it corrects. Its due has no floor and no late charge. A steward can move
56	 * a DRAFT, OPEN or PENDING claim to another person: it keeps its date, takes the next number (a
