58	 * a statement bound it to, and is listed as its new person's newest claim. A steward can re-settle
59	 * a SETTLED claim: its due is fixed again at the figure it would have today as an open claim bound
60	 * by no statement (today's rates, grades, floor and late charge). An OPEN claim can be deferred to
61	 * a date after the sheet's today: until the sheet's today reaches it the claim counts in no total,
62	 * is not overdue, cannot be settled and is left unbound by a statement; from then on it is an OPEN
63	 * claim like any other. A claim has a proofs count, raised by one at a time while it is not SETTLED
64	 * or VOID. An OPEN claim can be split: an amount split off it becomes a new OPEN claim (see
65	 * {@link #split}). A claim whose figure is above the proof threshold in force on its date cannot be settled
66	 * or approved while it has no proofs: that is refused before the clerk limit is considered. A claim
67	 * whose due is above the note threshold in force on its date cannot be opened while its note is empty.
68	 * Who may open, settle, void or move a claim is the sheet's permission matrix (see
69	 * {@link Sheet#permits}): an action the user's role may not take is refused (403). When a claim is
70	 * settled, approved or re-settled, each user watching its person is notified, in the order they
71	 * started watching. A steward may void a SETTLED claim within {@value #VOID_SETTLED_DAYS} days of its
72	 * settlement (the date its status log records it SETTLED) by the sheet's today: it keeps its number and
73	 * its frozen figure, which leaves every total. A DRAFT claim can be deleted (DELETED: it counts nowhere
74	 * and cannot be edited, opened or voided), and restored to DRAFT on the sheet-today it was deleted.
75	 */
76	@Service
77	public class ClaimService {
78	
